############################################################
# Body
############################################################

BEGIN_PGML
Let [`g(x)=\frac{1}{s\sqrt{2\pi}}e^{-\frac{(x-m)^2}{2s^2}}\text{,}`] where [`s>0\text{.}`] Find the range of [`x`] values for which [`g'(x)`] is positive.

[_]{$checks}{5}

END_PGML

############################################################
# Solution
############################################################

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
The constant factor [`\frac{1}{s\sqrt{2\pi}}`] is positive. Differentiating the exponential part gives

[```
                    \begin{aligned}
                    g'(x)
                    &= \frac{1}{s\sqrt{2\pi}}e^{-\frac{(x-m)^2}{2s^2}}
                    \left(-\frac{x-m}{s^2}\right).
                    \end{aligned}
                    ```]

The exponential factor is always positive, so the sign of [`g'(x)`] is determined by [`-(x-m)\text{.}`] Therefore, [`g'(x)>0`] when [`x<m\text{.}`]

END_PGML_SOLUTION

